              "text": "<p>Contact Stryker's customer service or technical support at 1 800 327 0770.</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Nov 16 2021 19:53:55 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys1": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 1,
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-98fdffe29c@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Jul 11 2019 15:25:15 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Height: 3.4 inches<br>\n Width: 9.2 inches <br>\n Depth: 10.9 inches&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Fri May 27 2022 17:08:56 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys2": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 2,
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-9846ac1203@example.invalid",
              "hideComponent": "false",
              "jcr:created": "Fri Jun 28 2019 14:11:17 GMT+0000",
              "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The LIFEPAK 1000 weighs 7.1 pounds with one set of REDI-PAK electrodes and one non-rechargeable battery.&nbsp;</span><br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Jul 11 2022 15:24:22 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys3": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 3,
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-98fdffe29c@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Fri Jun 28 2019 14:11:17 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>AED</b> - Provides operating capability for basic users<br>\n <b>Manual </b>- Provides operating capability for advanced users<br>\n <b>ECG</b> - Provides ECG display capability with 3-wire ECG cable<br>\n <b>Setup</b> - Allows user to configure the device<br>\n <b>Data transfer </b>- Allows user to transfer patient data<br>\n <b>Auto test </b>- Provides daily automatic test of hardware and software&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Fri May 27 2022 17:09:49 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys4": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 4,
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-9846ac1203@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Fri Jun 28 2019 14:11:17 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Initial CPR</b> - User defined time for CPR after first analysis regardless of analysis decision. This setting can be set to OFF, 15, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120 and 180 seconds.<br>\n <b>Pre-shock CPR</b> - Allows for CPR while device is charging. This setting can be set to OFF, 15 or 30 seconds.<br>\n <b>Stacked shocks</b> - This setting can be set to ON or OFF. When set to OFF, this allows for provision of CPR after each shock.<br>\n <b>Pulse check </b>- This setting allows the device to prompt for a pulse check after every shock, after every NSA pulse check or never prompt for a pulse check. The default setting is NEVER.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Jul 11 2022 15:24:42 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordionsGrid": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "1": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": "1",
              "accTitle": "What are the physical dimensions of the LIFEPAK 1000?"
            },
            "2": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": "2",
              "accTitle": "How much does the LIFEPAK 1000 weigh? "
            },
            "3": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": "3",
              "accTitle": "What are the six device modes in the LIFEPAK 1000? "
            },
            "4": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": "4",
              "accTitle": "What are the cprMAX technology settings? "
            },
            "5": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": 5,
              "accTitle": "What is the energy sequence for the LIFEPAK 1000? "
            },
            "6": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "accPosId": 6,
              "accTitle": "What are the ECG options for the LIFEPAK 1000?  "
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys5": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 5,
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-98fdffe29c@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Jul 11 2019 15:25:15 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The default energy output settings are 200, 300, 360 joules and then 360 joules for every shock thereafter.</span></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Fri May 27 2022 17:10:42 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "accordion_parsys6": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "accPosId": 6,
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-98fdffe29c@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Jul 11 2019 15:25:15 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">ECG information is received from the adult and infant/child electrodes in anterior-lateral or anterior-posterior positions. A three-wire cable can be used for ECG monitoring (Lead II).</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Waveform sweep speed</b> - 25 mm/sec for ECG, nominal <br>\n <b>Waveform viewing time</b> - Minimum four seconds<br>\n <b>Waveform amplitude</b> - 1 cm/mV, nominal<br>\n <b>Heart rate</b> - 20 to 300 BPM digital display&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Aug 29 2022 16:36:37 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
